From dcb00695a3e3a250db6605c5a7894151b47d7e92 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Pranit Rane <pranitrane@google.com>
Date: Thu, 18 Jun 2026 21:26:29 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] TelephonyProvider: Fix SQL injection in projection and
 sortOrder

Fix SQL injection vulnerability in TelephonyProvider (SmsProvider, MmsProvider, and MmsSmsProvider) which allowed apps with READ_SMS permission to extract sensitive SMS and OTP content.

Remediation details:
1. Enable strict query validation (setStrict(true)) and strict grammar check (setStrictGrammar(true)) on SQLiteQueryBuilder instances used to handle queries with user-supplied parameters. This protects against parentheses escape injection in selection clauses.
2. Enhance SqlQueryChecker's blocklist in Java to intercept and reject potentially dangerous SQL keywords (e.g. SELECT, UNION, JOIN) and SQL functions (e.g. HEX, SUBSTR, SQLITE_VERSION) used for data extraction, while allowing standard aggregate functions (e.g. COUNT).
3. Rename SqlQueryChecker validation methods (e.g. checkQueryParametersForDisallowedTokens) to reflect the generic blocklist covering functions and keywords.
4. Add SqlQueryCheckerTest.java unit tests to verify the validation rules.
5. Add validation unit tests in MmsProviderTest and MmsSmsProviderTest to verify subquery block behavior under restricted access.

Bug: 494725584
Flag: EXEMPT BUGFIX
Test: atest CtsTelephonyProviderTestCases TelephonyProviderTests
